	Section:
		Text: Text formatting
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Ligatures
		Paragraph: Some fonts have one glyph for a pair of letters such as fi or fl, and the engine uses those of the font: fi in IBM Plex Sans, fi and fl in IBM Plex Serif. With `Ligatures: false`, each letter is its own glyph. The text that is read or copied has the letters, and a `Letter spacing` other than 0 turns the ligatures off.
